  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe reported bug does not reproduce, so there is no code change. Instead, new tests pin the contract the issue asks for.\n\n- **How setup order is stored:** it is the name order. `setup::setups` reads `model::named_entities`, which sorts by name. No index field, list component or entity-id order holds it. When undo re-spawns a deleted setup, it sorts back into its old place. The operation order (`setup::operation_order`, ranked by setup) and the post follow from that.\n- **Where the report came from:** PR #1361's MCP test made \"Front\" then \"Back\" and saw `[\"Back\", \"Front\"]` after the undo. That was already the order before the delete (name order, not creation order). The setup did not move.\n- New suite `crates/app/tests/setup_delete_order.rs`:\n  - `undoing_delete_of_a_middle_setup_restores_its_place_and_the_program` sets up three setups, created out of name order (`A_First`, `C_Last`, then `B_Middle`). Each has its own stock, and Face ops sit in the first and last. It deletes `B_Middle` and undoes, then asserts the setup names, the active setup, the operation order, and that the **full posted G-code text** equals the program posted before the delete. It then redoes, which deletes the setup again, and undoes again.\n  - `undoing_delete_of_the_first_setup_puts_it_back_first` checks that the setup `None` resolves to comes back first after undo.\n- `docs/decisions/1362-delete-setup-undo-order.md` records this finding.\n\n## Related commands checked\n\n- `CreateSetup` undo removes the setup it made.\n- A datum-transfer clone is a `CreateSetup`; its undo is pinned by `setups::datum_transfer_clones_the_world_and_undoes_exactly`.\n- Main has no setup reorder or setup rename command, so nothing else can move a setup.\n- If an explicit, hand-set setup position is added later, these tests fail when its undo loses the position.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green. It ran app:`setup_delete_order` (2 passed).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --tests -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Both tests also pass on unchanged main, which is the finding.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- GUI Setups page. It lists through the same `setup::names`.\n- MCP `delete_setup`. That tool is in the unmerged PR #1361; its test could drop the `sort()`.\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0; upstream/main merged into the branch.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: high (issue labelled effort:medium; worked by issue-worker-high; no escalation)\n\nFixes #1362\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
